# Hot reload R2 (SparksReload LC7b): fields move by name or @formerly when the type and shape text
# match; a written field keeps its value, an unwritten one takes the new default (writes in Enable
# count); a changed type, struct layout or enum case list loses the value; removed and changed held
# fields stop their resources; handler connections keep their order and new `on` handlers go last; an
# execution that uses a removed field (directly or through a callee) is cancelled even with keep, and
# a kept execution writes fields whose offsets moved in two reloads; a disabled instance gets no
# connections; a faulting new `$init` (here: the instruction budget) refuses the reload unchanged.
